I'm guessing that there is a difference for those suffering from
the heartbreak of proportional fonts as defaults. To cater for
them, you might consider making the opening page monster list a
table, with the opening bullet, the symbol, and the descriptive
text/monster name in three separate columns, the bullet centered
horizontally, the monster letter centered horizontally, and the
descriptive text left justified, in their respective text cells.

I'm a bit of a typesetting fanatic, having written quite a bit of
type setting code for pay over the years, and the ragged left
border of the (proposed third column) monster names jumped off the
screen and kicked me in the eyeball, in Mozilla 1.7b with all
text settings still at default as delivered.

Some of us are a bit sensitive!

I'm guessing that shifting to a table would fix that.

[Probably actually, shifting to a fixed pitch font for just the
monster letter, including the space character, would fix that,
but the raw HTML would be hideous, with a font shift in and out
for each line of the table, unless there's a style sheet trick
